            "text": "{\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application and either the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality or the evidence of identity must be documented through the submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section, subject to an exception for married names.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C))\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [\n        \"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"exception\",\n      \"meaning\": \"An exception to the requirement to document material name discrepancies applies to married names as provided in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(1) Court orders or decrees:\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [\n        \"Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"alternative\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Under 22 CFR 51.25, court orders or decrees are an acceptable means of documenting a material name change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(a) Name change orders; or\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [\n        \"Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\",\n        \"(1) Court orders or decrees:\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"alternative\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Under court orders or decrees, name change orders constitute an acceptable means of documenting a material name change per 22 CFR 51.25.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(b) Divorce decrees;\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [\n        \"Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\",\n        \"(1) Court orders or decrees:\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"alternative\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Under court orders or decrees, divorce decrees constitute an acceptable means of documenting a material name change per 22 CFR 51.25.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(2) Certificates of naturalization;\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [\n        \"Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"alternative\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Per 22 CFR 51.25, certificates of naturalization constitute an acceptable means of documenting a material name change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(3) Marriage certificates;\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [\n        \"Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"alternative\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Per 22 CFR 51.25, marriage certificates constitute an acceptable means of documenting a material name change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [\n        \"Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"alternative\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Per 22 CFR 51.25, documentation demonstrating a change of name by operation of state law constitutes an acceptable means of documenting a material name change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(5) Documentation of customary usage.\",\n      \"scope_quotes\": [\n        \"Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"alternative\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Per 22 CFR 51.25, documentation of customary usage constitutes an acceptable means of documenting a material name change.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
